course: dictionary
lesson: 14284
title: Noticed, famous, important
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Notable» means worth noticing, or important enough to be noticed. «The museum has a notable collection of old coins.» The coins are special and worth looking at, so notable means worth noticing.
explain: «Notable» can also mean famous or well known. «Marie Curie was a notable scientist.» She is famous, so notable here means well known.
explain: As a noun, «notables» is a formal word for important or famous people. «The mayor welcomed the notables to the town hall.» The notables are the important guests, not just any people.
explain: A «notable exception» is one that does not follow the usual pattern. «Most days were cloudy, but Monday was a notable exception.» Monday did not follow the pattern, and it stood out.
fact: «Notable» is an adjective, so it can change to «more notable».
fact: «Notable» means worth noticing or important.
fact: «Notable» can mean famous or well known, as in «a notable writer».
fact: As a formal noun, «a notable» is an important or famous person.
fact: «A notable exception» is one that does not follow the usual pattern.
exercise: «The fire crew received a notable award for bravery.» What does notable mean here? | *Important enough to be noticed | Quiet and shy | Very small and hard to see | Cheap and old
exercise: Mia says «notable» means forgettable. Why is she wrong? | *Notable means worth noticing, the opposite of forgettable | Notable means forgettable, so she is right | Notable means a type of bird | Notable means very loud
exercise: «Most of the class passed, with one notable exception.» What is a notable exception? | A very small mistake | A rule that everyone must follow | A kind teacher | *One that does not follow the usual pattern
test: «The town is notable for its tall clock tower.» What is the town known for? | Its loud trains | Its many dogs | *Its tall clock tower | Its heavy rain
test: «The notables sat at the front of the hall.» Find and copy the word that means important or famous people. | front | *notables | sat | hall
exam: «The speech was notable, so everyone wrote it down.» What does notable suggest? | Spoken in a foreign language | *Worth noticing and remembering | Too long to finish | Written in pencil
